    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I never really liked math beyond the basics. As a primary school graduate, I remember learning addition and subtraction, but anything beyond that felt confusing. I’ve always found it hard to follow the logic or patterns. I respect it as a tool used in economics and biology, but I don’t feel connected to it personally.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, especially when I hear about complex topics like calculus or statistics. I worry that I’m missing something simple, and that I’ll be unable to keep up. My anxiety comes from not having a strong foundation, and the fear of making a mistake—especially when I’m trying to understand something new.",
